# Destructive ops — intent (hooks enforce)

Hooks are tripwires. Real safety = least privilege + backups agent cannot delete.

## Never (agent must not try)

- Force-push / rewrite `master`/`main`; `git reset --hard`; `git clean -fd`
- `rm -rf` outside workspace, `$HOME`, `/`, or with unexpanded variables
- Touch `/opt/bizarre-prod`, `/var/lib/bizarre`, `/etc/bizarre`, or `prod.env`
- SSH to Proxmox hosts (`pve` / `pve2`) or `root@*`
- Edit or delete `.cursor/hooks.json` / `.cursor/hooks/**` (self-protection)
- DROP DATABASE/SCHEMA; `mkfs`; `dd` to block devices

## Prod triage (CT 103 / bizarre-api)

- Diagnose as **agent user** only — logs + read-only SQL. No writes to prod tree/media/env.
- Fixes land on **madvillainy** (or `/opt/bizarre` agent tree) → PR → deploy. Do not hot-edit prod.
- Prefer `git worktree remove` over `rm` for worktrees.

## Ask human first

- `ssh`/`scp` to `bizarre-api-agent`
- Recursive delete inside repo; `pg_restore`; `sudo`; service restart
- `ALLOW_PROD_DB=1` (should not be needed if agent has no prod write creds)

## Operator checklist (not agent work)

- Off auto-run for terminal; dedicated local ed25519 agent key on madvillainy
- GitHub ruleset: no force-push / no branch delete on `master`
- Nightly DB+media backup off-host (PBS/restic append-only); pre-session `pct snapshot`
